pacity, which can help confirm the second wind phenomenon in McArdle disease patients.", "BIOPSIA MUSCULAR:Muscle biopsy is a diagnostic procedure that can show focal accumulations of normal glycogen and assess enzyme activity in patients with McArdle disease.", "EJERCICIO AERÓBICO LIGERO-MODERADO:Light to moderate aerobic exercise is recommended for patients with McArdle disease to improve physical fitness and increase muscle oxidative capacity.", "GSDVI:Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI) is a rare metabolic disorder characterized by a mutation in the liver isoform of glycogen phosphorylase. This condition is similar to Glycogen Storage Disease Type IX (GSDIX) and necessitates dietary management to address liver-related issues. Individuals with GSDVI often experience symptoms such as hepatomegaly and hypoglycemia, particularly in early childhood.", "PYGL:The PYGL gene is responsible for encoding the liver isoform of glycogen phosphorylase, which is crucial for glycogenolysis.", "GLYCOGEN PHOSPHORYLASE:Glycogen phosphorylase is the enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate, playing a key role in glucose metabolism.", "AMNIOCENTESIS:Amniocentesis is a medical procedure utilized for prenatal diagnosis, allowing for the analysis of amniotic fluid to detect various genetic conditions. This procedure can be employed to identify galactosemia, a metabolic disorder, as well as to detect the mutation associated with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI). Through the examination of the amniotic fluid, healthcare providers can gain valuable insights into the genetic health of the fetus.", "GSDIX:GSDIX is a condition that primarily affects the liver and is classified as the most common glycogen storage disease, with an estimated prevalence of 1 in 100,000 individuals. This condition arises from mutations in genes that code for phosphorylase b kinase, which plays a crucial role in glycogen metabolism. To manage the symptoms of GSDIX, particularly hypoglycemia, specific dietary treatments are required.", "PHKA2:PHKA2 is a gene located on the X chromosome that codes for the hepatic isoform of the alpha subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXa.", "PHKB:PHKB is a gene located on chromosome 16 that codes for the beta subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXb.", "PHKG2:PHKG2 is a gene located on chromosome 16 that codes for the gamma subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXc."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}